# These guides are packaged verbatim into the handoff zip, and that zip's sha256
# is quoted as its identity.
#
# A .docx is a ZIP of XML parts, so it is binary as far as git is concerned.
# Without this rule git can apply end-of-line conversion to it, which corrupts
# the archive outright, and would in any case make the package hash differently
# on a fresh clone than it does here. Same lesson as operator-notebooks, one
# severity worse: there the bytes changed, here the file stops opening.
*.docx binary
